 "notes": "LAMPOST prototype optical haloscope search for dark photon dark matter (kinetic mixing epsilon = chi). Curve is the boundary of the magenta 'Limit from this work' shaded region in Fig. 4 (file kfig3.pdf), the paper's headline 90% CL limit. Extracted as vector data from the stroked outline via get_drawings; axes calibrated on the log-log tick labels (x: mA'/eV, y: epsilon). The region is a narrow bathtub over mass 0.70-0.82 eV with minimum epsilon ~ 8e-13 near 0.73 eV; excluded region lies above the curve. Points where the spike exits the top of the frame (epsilon > ~1e-11) were clipped. Local DM density rho_DM = 0.4 GeV/cm^3 assumed by the paper (not rescaled per task card). The thin purple '90% SDE' curve is a projection for an improved detector, not reported. chi reported directly (paper works with epsilon, not epsilon^2).",
